# BooKoo Project Rules

The full rulebook lives in the two root documents. Read them; they are the
source of truth and this rule only restates their headline constraints.

@AGENTS.md
@CLAUDE.md

## The hard rules, in short

1. **Unbounded lists paginate.** `FlashList` + `paginationOptsValidator` +
   `usePaginatedQuery` + `onEndReached`. Never `ScrollView + map`, never an
   uncapped `.collect()`, never a whole-collection `useQuery`. Add the index
   before the pagination.
2. **`any` is banned.** Concrete types, `unknown`, generics or type guards.
   Convex ids are `Id<'tableName'>` from `convex/_generated/dataModel`.
   `as any` / `as unknown as T` to dodge a type error is the same violation.
3. **expo-router routes are typed.** String literals, no cast. A typed-route
   error means the route file is missing — create it.
4. **i18n keys are static literals.** Branch with `if`/`switch`;
   `t(dynamicKey as any)` is forbidden.
5. **Money is an integer in minor units** with an ISO 4217 currency string.
   Timestamps are epoch-ms numbers; month keys `'YYYY-MM'`, day keys
   `'YYYY-MM-DD'`.
6. **Performance is the acceptance criterion.** Every query is index-bounded,
   every dashboard number comes from a rollup, membership checks are O(1).
   See `CLAUDE.md` → PERFORMANCE.
7. **Reusable UI belongs to cpk-ui.** Consume or improve its public primitives;
   add missing controls and charts upstream instead of implementing competing
   visuals in BooKoo. BooKoo owns only domain adapters and screen composition.
   See `src/AGENTS.md` for the cross-repository, native/web, test, and local-link
   workflow.
8. **cpk-ui Button radius is a prop.** `borderRadius={8}` on `Button` /
   `BookooButton`. Never put `borderRadius` or `padding` in `style`. Padding
   belongs in `styles.container`. A loading overlay must use the same radius.

Directory-scoped rules: `convex/AGENTS.md`, `app/AGENTS.md`, `src/AGENTS.md`,
`shared/AGENTS.md`, `scripts/AGENTS.md`.

This file is hand-authored. The `00-` prefix keeps
`.agents/scripts/sync-skills.sh` from pruning it — the prune loop skips
`.cursor/rules/` files whose basename matches `[0-9][0-9]-*`.
